// A source that performs the operation of an `extern` block in another source.
// `round-trip.gandr` declares the block `Boundary`, and this source declares
// no block.
//
// A program keeps its Rust boundary in one source. Each other source performs
// the boundary's operations through an import of that source, and it writes no
// copy of the block.
//
// The import opens the block's interface. A row here names `Boundary`, and a
// call performs `Boundary.add`. The run offers each perform to the Rust
// caller's host, as it does for `quadrupled`. The block's row check runs at the
// block's own source alone.
//
// - see: `model/interop/boundary/round-trip.gandr` — the block and
//   `quadrupled`
// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs` — the Rust caller

// `Boundary` and `quadrupled`.
import "./round-trip.gandr";

/// Sixteen times its argument: `quadrupled`, then two adds of the sum to
/// itself.
pub def sixteenfold(x : u32) -> [Boundary] u32 =
  let y = quadrupled x
  let z = Boundary.add y y
  Boundary.add z z
